OS 4.0
\ Records when the disk fails: the copy holding the last durable record is never overwritten  ok
create r1 100 allot  ok
: show ( -- ) r1 100 40 record@ r1 swap type space ;  ok
: broken ( xt -- n ) data-disk @ >r 99 data-disk ! catch r> data-disk ! ;  ok
s" first" 40 record!  show  40 copy-seq .  41 copy-seq . first 0 1  ok
: put2 ( -- ) s" second" 40 record! ;  : put3 ( -- ) s" third" 40 record! ;  ok
' put2 broken .  ' put3 broken . -34 -34  ok
40 copy-seq .  41 copy-seq . 2 1  ok
\ a crash now loses the cache: the durable record is still there  ok
empty-buffers show first  ok
s" fourth" 40 record!  empty-buffers show  40 copy-seq .  41 copy-seq . fourth 2 1  ok
' put2 broken .  s" fifth" 40 record!  empty-buffers show  40 copy-seq .  41 copy-seq . -34 fifth 4 3  ok
\ a disk that cannot be written: RECORD! fails, and RECORD@ never reads what it failed to write (defect 39)  ok
: put6 ( -- ) s" sixth" 40 record! ;  false disk-ok !  ' put6 catch .  true disk-ok !  show  empty-buffers show -258 fifth fifth  ok
: put0 ( -- ) s" zero" 0 record! ;  ' put0 catch .  ' put0 catch .  0 block 8 type 0 -259 OS40DISK ok
\ sequence numbers wrap (defect 40): a copy numbered 2^64-1 is older than the next  ok
: forge ( addr len seq n -- ) ['] fill-copy blocks-lock locked sync ;  ok
s" newest" -1 50 forge  s" older" -2 51 forge  r1 100 50 record@ r1 swap type space newest  ok
s" after" 50 record!  50 copy-seq .  51 copy-seq .  r1 100 50 record@ r1 swap type space -1 1 after  ok
s" next" 50 record!  50 copy-seq .  51 copy-seq .  r1 100 50 record@ r1 swap type space 2 1 next  ok
s" low" 1 60 forge  s" high" -1 61 forge  s" new" 60 record!  60 copy-seq .  61 copy-seq .  r1 100 60 record@ r1 swap type 1 2 new ok
